You can try to use `Text` component in `FlowLayout` to achieve this effect. It will be a bit tricky, since `FlowLayout` doesn't have a direct way to align text horizontally.

Here's an example:

```java
import javax.swing.*;
import java.awt.*;

public class HorizontalAlignmentExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() -> {
            JFrame frame = new JFrame("Horizontal Alignment Example");
            frame.setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE);
            frame.setSize(300, 200);

            JPanel panel = new JPanel(new FlowLayout(FlowLayout.LEFT));
            panel.add(new Text("First text"));
            panel.add(new Text("Second text"));
            panel.add(new Text("Third text"));

            frame.add(panel);
            frame.setVisible(true);
        });
    }

    static class Text extends JPanel {
        public Text(String text) {
            super(new BorderLayout());
            JLabel label = new JLabel(text);
            label.setHorizontalAlignment(JLabel.LEFT);
            add(label);
        }
    }
}
```

